{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/5485-giant-merit","id":5485,"title":"Giant Merit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-07T15:35:05-08:00","id":5485,"title":"Giant Merit","content":"It seems a little too... costly, the Giant Merit. As it stands in GMC it's still a 3 dot merit, and all it does is increase Size by 1 to give you a grand total of +1 to health. It seems a little too expensive to me. Does anyone else think so?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T15:42:46-08:00","id":5491,"title":"","content":"One Health box is pretty dandy. I might argue for the merit to cost 2 Dots instead, but it's hardly a massive issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T15:50:37-08:00","id":5502,"title":"","content":"Well, I tend to give some sort of other minor bonuses (I currently have a PC that is a Giant ex-boxer). Those I remind, I gave a bonus to Intimidation (he was using physical threats and so rolling Strength + Intimidation and thought the Size will matter) and on rolls to move/lift and push objects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T18:50:51-08:00","id":5653,"title":"","content":"By the RAW Size effects more than Health. There's all sorts of little rules here and there. Size helps you with some Athletics rolls, and resist some Tilts, as examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T18:56:50-08:00","id":5661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/5485-giant-merit?p=5653#post5653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the RAW Size effects more than Health. There's all sorts of little rules here and there. Size helps you with some Athletics rolls, and resist some Tilts, as examples.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can I get some page numbers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T20:16:32-08:00","id":5699,"title":"","content":"The &quot;species factor&quot; for Speed has also been replaced with Size, so that human Speed is Size + Strength + Dexterity. So it's +1 Speed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T01:50:51-08:00","id":5773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/5485-giant-merit?p=5661#post5661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can I get some page numbers?</div> </div> </div> </div>WOD:<br /> <br /> Jumping pages 66-67.<br /> <br /> Falling objects page 138 (though this is lower of Size and Armor, so Armor is almost always going to be more important).<br /> <br /> Life falling objects, Size matters at ST discretion on vehicle on person collisions if the person is sufficiently tough enough compared to the vehicle.<br /> <br /> GMC:<br /> <br /> The Stunned Tilt is checked against the target's Size, so more Size means you're harder to stun. Page 212.<br /> <br /> Size is also used to measure how much you can take from a stun gun; page 240.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T06:13:48-08:00","id":5858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/5485-giant-merit?p=5699#post5699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;species factor&quot; for Speed has also been replaced with Size, so that human Speed is Size + Strength + Dexterity. So it's +1 Speed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does it say this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T12:15:57-08:00","id":6231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/5485-giant-merit?p=5858#post5858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where does it say this?</div> </div> </div> </div>...turns out it doesn'! Not in GMC, anyway. But p.5, Reap the Whirlwind says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Speed is Size + Strength + Dexterity. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T15:18:34-08:00","id":6402,"title":"","content":"Ops, well I already said my Vampire players that it worked that way. Accidental House-Rule, those things happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T11:46:58-07:00","id":1062401,"title":"","content":"Am I crazy or does &quot;Size 6 and +1 health&quot; not insinuate that you get a total of +2 health, since clearly size 6 raises your health by 1 on its own?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13130-tempestsatori","name":"TempestSatori","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T11:54:34-07:00","id":1062407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempestSatori</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/5485-giant-merit?p=1062401#post1062401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I crazy or does &amp;quot;Size 6 and +1 health&amp;quot; not insinuate that you get a total of +2 health, since clearly size 6 raises your health by 1 on its own?</div> </div> </div> </div>The +1 health part is reminder text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T11:57:14-07:00","id":1062410,"title":"","content":"Species factor vs size is one of the more inconsistent rules in Chronicles. Half the books say one, half say the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T12:04:48-07:00","id":1062416,"title":"","content":"I think you're thinking about Speed where humans (and their variations) use Size while all other beings use a species factor. Health is always Stamina + Size.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T14:12:18-07:00","id":1062474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/5485-giant-merit?p=5491#post5491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One Health box is pretty dandy. I might argue for the merit to cost 2 Dots instead, <b>but it's hardly a massive issue.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>HA!<br /> <br /> anyhow, on one hand, yeah, Giant should probably be cheaper, but I'm glad it's 3 instead of 4 (how it was in NWoD) and I figure the expense is less about how valuable it is, and more about how rare it is...Giant doesn't just mean you're tall, but like...exceptionally tall. 6'6&quot; to 7 feet tall, or more. It's not unheard of, but it's certainly not something every character ought to have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T15:16:25-07:00","id":1062494,"title":"","content":"The thing is, it doesn't just give you an extra dot of health. It permanently increases your maximum health by one.<br /> <br /> A giant character's HP goes to 11. <br /> <br /> Also mages need to work harder to cast spells on you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T15:24:54-07:00","id":1062500,"title":"","content":"Makes me think of my co-player's Gangrel character with maxed Resilience who has the Giant Merit, gains +1 Size from his Bloodline when in &quot;true form&quot;, and adds another +1 Size when using the Force of Nature Devotion in battle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T15:26:53-07:00","id":1062501,"title":"","content":"Giant is good at 3 Dots for the plethora of little benefits it gives you. None of them stand out dramatically except the bonus health, but they are hidden all over the place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T15:36:23-07:00","id":1062506,"title":"","content":"Yeah, being outside the default Scale Factor of Mage spells is one example of a not immediately obvious but still highly useful benefit of being Giant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T20:29:14-07:00","id":1062630,"title":"","content":"I dunno, I don't read that as reminder text. If it was, it'd be something more like &quot;She is Size 6, and as a result has +1 Health&quot;.<br /> <br /> What is says is &quot;She is Size 6, and has +1 Health&quot;. That seems pretty clear to me - your character is Size 6, and gets an extra health level <i>on top of</i> the extra one you get from increased Size.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T20:44:58-07:00","id":1062642,"title":"","content":"In 1ed I house ruled that size 6 meant your human maximum strength was 6, meaning not only was it possible to raise your strength to 6 but the 5th dot didn't cost double. 2ed eliminated the doubled cost but I still think raising the maximum to 6 would be acceptable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T01:15:05-07:00","id":1062704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/5485-giant-merit?p=1062630#post1062630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, I don't read that as reminder text. If it was, it'd be something more like &quot;She is Size 6, and as a result has +1 Health&quot;.<br /> <br /> What is says is &quot;She is Size 6, and has +1 Health&quot;. That seems pretty clear to me - your character is Size 6, and gets an extra health level <i>on top of</i> the extra one you get from increased Size.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I run it that way. Makes the merit semi-worth it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T01:41:09-07:00","id":1062707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/5485-giant-merit?p=1062630#post1062630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, I don't read that as reminder text. If it was, it'd be something more like &amp;quot;She is Size 6, and as a result has +1 Health&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> What is says is &amp;quot;She is Size 6, and has +1 Health&amp;quot;. That seems pretty clear to me - your character is Size 6, and gets an extra health level <i>on top of</i> the extra one you get from increased Size.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree that it could be interpreted that way, but it's clearly not the intent. The 1e version was 1 dot more and more clearly worded - it said &quot;Your character is seven or more feet tall and over 250 pounds. He is +1 Size (and thus +1 Health).&quot; Similarly, Small Framed in 2e says, &quot;Your character is diminutive. He\u2019s not five feet, and it\u2019s easy to walk into him without noticing. He\u2019s Size 4, and thus has one fewer Health box.&quot; I imagine if the intent had been to double the health granting benefit while reducing the cost of Giant, that the wording would have been more unambiguously differentiated, for example saying, &quot;She is size 6, and has +1 health (in addition to the increased Health due to her Size).&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/5485-giant-merit?p=1062704#post1062704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I run it that way. Makes the merit semi-worth it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's already a full experience cheaper than increasing your Stamina, which is the only other mundane way to increase Health.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T01:46:50-07:00","id":1062708,"title":"","content":"I don't feel that 25 percent discount on the cost of raising a Stamina by 1 more is worth gaining only one effect of increased Stamina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T02:02:11-07:00","id":1062711,"title":"","content":"Increased Size has multiple benefits besides increasing your Health. While a some of these weren't converted to 2e (such as Size boosting in certain Athletics rolls), having more Size makes it easier to win physical Chases, and makes you harder to Stun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T09:34:14-07:00","id":1062827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/5485-giant-merit?p=1062407#post1062407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The +1 health part is reminder text.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Is there any other place where &quot;reminder text&quot; like that is in the book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13130-tempestsatori","name":"TempestSatori","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T09:44:29-07:00","id":1062832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempestSatori</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/5485-giant-merit?p=1062827#post1062827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any other place where &amp;quot;reminder text&amp;quot; like that is in the book?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like what?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T10:01:04-07:00","id":1062843,"title":"","content":"I'm 99% sure this was clarified by a writer at some point but I can't find the thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T10:07:43-07:00","id":1062849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/5485-giant-merit?p=1062843#post1062843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm 99% sure this was clarified by a writer at some point but I can't find the thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I went through the same process. The closest I can find is that in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/94732-giant-merit\">this one</a> where David answers why the height of Giant changed from &quot;seven or more feet&quot; to &quot;well over six feet&quot;. I would think, given that the general consensus in the thread was that +1 health was the intent, and he came to the thread to clarify a point, he would have also mentioned if that consensus was incorrect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T11:22:14-07:00","id":1062877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/5485-giant-merit?p=1062849#post1062849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I went through the same process. The closest I can find is that in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/94732-giant-merit\">this one</a> where David answers why the height of Giant changed from &quot;seven or more feet&quot; to &quot;well over six feet&quot;. I would think, given that the general consensus in the thread was that +1 health was the intent, and he came to the thread to clarify a point, he would have also mentioned if that consensus was incorrect.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no doubt <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13130-tempestsatori\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13130\" data-vbnamecard=\"13130\">TempestSatori</a> that Giant merit grants +1 health, not +2. You gain the health due to increased size. As always the ST may rule something different if he or she has a feeling that the merit is underpowered, but IMO increased size is a bit more than just +1 health. However for many players buying resilience seems more reasonable","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T12:14:59-07:00","id":1062905,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12872\" data-vbnamecard=\"12872\">Edgar McAlister</a> You <i>do</i> realize that not everyone gets access to Resilience, right? Also, the simple fact that someone disagrees with you means that there is <i>some</i> doubt<i>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> That's... kind of besides the point, really. Giant may have done that in 1e, but that doesn't mean it does that in 2e - quite a lot of merits had their mechanics tweaked (see Allies for an example that changed <i>pretty drastically</i>).<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Small-Framed has an all-important word &quot;thus&quot;. Consider the following two sentences:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">1. &quot;She is Size 4, and thus has one fewer health box.&quot;<br /> 2. &quot;She is Size 4, and has one fewer health box.&quot;</div>Those two sentences can be reworded as follows, without changing their meaning:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">1a. &quot;She has one fewer health box as a result of being Size 4.&quot;<br /> 2a. &quot;She has one fewer health box, and is Size 4.&quot;</div>While Small-Framed is worded like sentence 1, Giant is worded like sentence 2. Another simple example (replacing &quot;one fewer health box&quot; with something more drastic):<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">1b. &quot;She is Size 4, and thus has red hair.&quot;<br /> 2b. &quot;She is Size 4, and has red hair.&quot;</div>Does sentence 2b state that she has red hair due to being Size 4? Does 2a imply that she's Size 4 due to having one fewer health level?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T12:35:51-07:00","id":1062923,"title":"","content":"Like I said, I don't disagree that the Merit can be read that way, I'm just confident that it is not the intent. And of course Merits have had their functions change from 1e to 2e, but I think that if the intent had been to change Giant so as to have it give +1 Size and a floating +1 Health on top of that, it would have been worded so as to make that abundantly and unambiguously clear. For example, by changing it to, &quot;She is Size 5, and has +1 Health (in addition to the +1 Health from her increased Size).&quot; A number of development choices make it clear that the 2e books were designed with people familiar with 1e in mind, and I doubt that they would have made such a change without clarifying in the text so as to avoid those familiar with 1e mistakenly assuming it works the same way as the 1e version.<br /> <br /> And, again, I think David would have corrected us in that thread I linked if we had come to the wrong conclusion, since he took the time to comment on the reason for the change in height.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T12:38:58-07:00","id":1062924,"title":"","content":"I am also pretty confident that Giant only gives +1 health, but I would not complain if my ST were to rule it as +2!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I also like allowing Giants to have Strength 6 naturally, but by that logic Small-Framed would only have a max of 4, and I feel like that &quot;merit&quot; kind of sucks enough already as it is....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T14:06:02-07:00","id":1062970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/5485-giant-merit?p=1062905#post1062905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12872\" data-vbnamecard=\"12872\">Edgar McAlister</a> You <i>do</i> realize that not everyone gets access to Resilience, right? Also, the simple fact that someone disagrees with you means that there is <i>some</i> doubt<i>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> That's... kind of besides the point, really. Giant may have done that in 1e, but that doesn't mean it does that in 2e - quite a lot of merits had their mechanics tweaked (see Allies for an example that changed <i>pretty drastically</i>).<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Small-Framed has an all-important word &quot;thus&quot;. Consider the following two sentences:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">1. &quot;She is Size 4, and thus has one fewer health box.&quot;<br /> 2. &quot;She is Size 4, and has one fewer health box.&quot;</div>Those two sentences can be reworded as follows, without changing their meaning:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">1a. &quot;She has one fewer health box as a result of being Size 4.&quot;<br /> 2a. &quot;She has one fewer health box, and is Size 4.&quot;</div>While Small-Framed is worded like sentence 1, Giant is worded like sentence 2. Another simple example (replacing &quot;one fewer health box&quot; with something more drastic):<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">1b. &quot;She is Size 4, and thus has red hair.&quot;<br /> 2b. &quot;She is Size 4, and has red hair.&quot;</div>Does sentence 2b state that she has red hair due to being Size 4? Does 2a imply that she's Size 4 due to having one fewer health level?</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't analyse the <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Resilience in terms of access. I just </span></span></span>summarized it is better for a player character from a Vampire player/ST perspective. I don't have any problem with fact that someone disagrees with me. You can play however you want. In the end, the most important thing is to enjoy your game. I guess that the developers' intent was it gives +1 health, due to the fact it worked that way for years in all Vampire editions I can remember (or maybe I'm wrong? Yep I know it is CoD forum, but I'm a big Vampire fan and sometimes forget about other settings people play).<br /> As it comes to the sentence analyse you're probably right, but IMO it's almost casuistry. The rules are simpler and the intention seems clear to me.<br /> Anyway the +1 health rule seems okay or slightly week for some characters while the +2 health giant looks overpowered to me, but do as you wish, it's your game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","user":"Edgar McAlister","date":". 03-15-2017, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T14:32:40-07:00","id":1062976,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1170_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1170\" data-vbnamecard=\"1170\">amechra</a> I must admit that the Resilience and Vampire arguments were stupid. I was procrastinating at work and forgot I wrote a post on Chronicles of Darkness forum, not Vampire the Requiem. Shame on me<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Nevertheless it's +1 health.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T17:52:08-07:00","id":1063051,"title":"","content":"Does Giant (and Small-Framed, I guess) also apply to alternate forms? Like, is a Giant Uratha also unusually large while in otherwise-normal-wolf Urhan form? And a Small-Framed one is more coyote-sized?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T18:27:25-07:00","id":1063070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/5485-giant-merit?p=1063051#post1063051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Giant (and Small-Framed, I guess) also apply to alternate forms? Like, is a Giant Uratha also unusually large while in otherwise-normal-wolf Urhan form? And a Small-Framed one is more coyote-sized?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say yes, since the size bonuses (and penalties) apply to your size as is when shapeshifting. So yes, a giant who turns Gauru is gonna be bigger than a regular old Gauru (which is still pretty big!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T18:39:16-07:00","id":1063074,"title":"","content":"Seconded that different werewolf forms would also have +1 Size. However, the animal forms from Beast's Skin (Protean 3) would probably not be bigger than usual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T18:48:23-07:00","id":1063075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/5485-giant-merit?p=1063074#post1063074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seconded that different werewolf forms would also have +1 Size. However, the animal forms from Beast's Skin (Protean 3) would probably not be bigger than usual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, werewolf forms apply modifiers to the character's base stats, where Protean 3 replaces the character's base stats with an animal's. So a size 6 Uratha would become a size 5 wolf in Urhan form, but a size 6 Gangrel would become a size 4 wolf in Beast's Skin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T02:33:56-07:00","id":1063162,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to imagine a Giant in Urhan and a small-framed person in Urshul standing side-by-side. By all rights, they should be the same size, but...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}